---
title: Pending and success feedback
description: Drive pending indicators and confirmation messages from Superforms' own stores — Formsnap renders the fields, Superforms owns the submission state.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

Users need to know the form is sending, and whether it worked. Both come from the `superForm` instance: `$submitting` is true while an enhanced submission is in flight, and `$message` renders whatever the action passed to `message(form, …)`. No Formsnap-specific subscription is involved.

## Set the message in the action

```ts title="src/routes/feedback/+page.server.ts"
import { fail } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import { message, superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { feedbackSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	form: await superValidate(zod(feedbackSchema)),
});

export const actions = {
	default: async ({ request }) => {
		const form = await superValidate(request, zod(feedbackSchema));

		if (!form.valid) return fail(400, { form });

		return message(form, "Answer received.");
	},
};
```

## Render pending and success state

Destructure the stores you need from the form instance and reference them with the `$` prefix. `$submitting` disables the button and swaps its label while the request runs; `$message` appears when the action returns one:

```svelte title="src/routes/feedback/+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";

	let { data } = $props();

	const form = superForm(untrack(() => data.form), { resetForm: false });
	// `submitting` is Superforms' own store for an in-flight enhanced submission.
	const { form: formData, enhance, message, submitting, delayed, timeout } = form;
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhance>
	<Field {form} name="answer" fieldErrors>
		<Control>
			{#snippet children({ props })}
				<Label>Answer</Label>
				<input {...props} bind:value={$formData.answer} />
			{/snippet}
		</Control>
		{#snippet description()}Pending state and confirmation both come from Superforms.{/snippet}
	</Field>

	<button type="submit" disabled={$submitting}>
		{#if $timeout}
			Still sending…
		{:else if $delayed}
			Sending…
		{:else}
			Send answer
		{/if}
	</button>
</form>

{#if $message}
	<output>{$message}</output>
{/if}
```

For work that runs after a result is applied — counting updates, resetting local UI — use Superforms' `onUpdated` option:

```ts title="src/routes/feedback/+page.svelte"
const form = superForm(untrack(() => data.form), {
	resetForm: false,
	onUpdated({ form: updated }) {
		if (updated.valid) {
			// The action result has been applied to the stores.
		}
	},
});
```

## How it works

- `$submitting` flips for the duration of an enhanced (`use:enhance`) submission. `$delayed` flips after a grace period (500 ms by default) so quick submissions never flash a spinner, and `$timeout` flips after a longer threshold (8 seconds by default) for "still working" messaging. Tune both with Superforms' `delayMs` and `timeoutMs` options.
- `$message` holds whatever the action returned via `message(form, …)` — text, or an object if you pass one.
- `onUpdated` runs after a form action result has been applied to the stores, valid or not.

<Callout type="warning">

All three pending stores only move for enhanced submissions. Without `use:enhance` the browser performs a full-page POST and there is no client-side pending state to render — keep the markup correct for the native path too.

</Callout>
